    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and verified. The build succeeds and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` feature: when more than 80 owners have already been created for the day, the created (and subsequently fetched) owner carries `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`.\n\nFollowing the existing pattern used for computed fields like `namesakeCount`, the warning is computed at create time and persisted, so it's returned identically on both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges:\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` boolean `bulkSignupWarning` property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` field (`bulk_signup_warning` column) with getter/setter.\n- **`schema.sql`** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped the field, defaulting `null` to `false` so the response is never null.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added `computeBulkSignupWarning(...)` which counts existing owners sharing the new owner's adjusted business-day `registrationDate` (the same \"today\" accumulation path as the daily-limit rule) and returns `true` when that count exceeds the threshold of 80. The result is set on the owner before it's saved.\n\n`AcceptanceTest` and the full test suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
